   "questions": [
    "Is REGISTRY_BASE_URL explicitly exempt from startup environment validation and from the startup RuntimeSettings snapshot, so the service must start when it is absent?",
    "After startup, does each Registry call observe the current process-environment value of REGISTRY_BASE_URL, or the value captured in startup RuntimeSettings?",
    "Is REGISTRY_BASE_URL excluded from startup loading and validation and read directly from the environment for every Registry call, or is its value captured and validated in RuntimeSettings at startup?",
    "Is REGISTRY_BASE_URL a live environment value read for every Registry call, or a start-up value captured and validated in RuntimeSettings, and does the new sentence explicitly override the older start-up rules for this variable?"
   ],
